# detail
Number of changes: 1

1. Modified | Implementation code block
   Changed the method body from directly sorting and returning or assigning values to issuing a deprecation warning and calling `self.sort_values(...)` to return the result.
   The original implementation included:

   * Conditional statement: verify that `na_position` was `'last'` or `'first'`, otherwise raise `ValueError`;
   * Assignment statement: sort `self._codes` and assign the result to `codes`;
   * Conditional statement: reverse `codes` when `ascending` was false;
   * Conditional statements: adjust the position of the `-1` code according to `na_mask`, `na_position`, and `ascending`;
   * Conditional statement: when `inplace` was true, update `self._codes` and return; otherwise, return a new `Categorical(...)`.

   The new implementation includes:

   * Function call: call `warn(...)` to issue a `FutureWarning`;
   * Return statement: return `self.sort_values(inplace=inplace, ascending=ascending, na_position=na_position)`.
